From: junkyard
Subject: [PATCH] display/common: port to android-mainline

Linux 6.18 -> android-mainline (7.3):

  * struct drm_atomic_state -> struct drm_atomic_commit (upstream
    5164f7e7ff8e, applied with the same sed).
  * drm_bridge_funcs.atomic_reset/drm_atomic_helper_bridge_reset ->
    atomic_create_state/drm_atomic_helper_bridge_create_state.
  * hex2bin()/bin2hex()/hex_to_bin() live in <linux/hex.h>; FB_BLANK_*
    needs <linux/fb.h> (no longer pulled in by backlight.h); FALSE -> false.
  * drm_panel_init() is static now (panels are expected to come from
    devm_drm_panel_alloc()). gs_panel embeds its drm_panel in a struct it
    allocates itself, so gs_panel.c carries jy_drm_panel_init(): the same
    field setup plus kref_init() with no container, so drm_panel_add()/
    drm_panel_remove() balance their get/put and never free the embedding
    struct -- the 6.18 lifetime model.
---
